I rarely genocide anything. The only situation in which I'd consider
genociding is the classic "surrounded by foos, one move,  3 hp left"
circumstance. Other than that, I consider a bit of a cheat. The
monsters don't get to use it on us, after all (and a good thing too!)

The most frequent targets of genocide are h and L. I have a very, very
high respect for both - I don't just mean respect as in "handle with
caution", but true respect as they embody (for me) what's most
interesting about Nethack. We need more, not fewer, monsters that fall
into the pattern of "wimpy standard combat attacks and therefore not
conventionally dangerous, but contains one short-range (melee) special
attack that is potentially deadly." If not for h and L (and green
slime/cockatrice to name two more), combat wombats would just be able
to plow their way through the surrounding monsters without even
thinking about what they're doing. Try meleeing a master mind flayer
just once (as I did) and you quickly are forced to rethink your combat
strategy, at least in some cases.

